                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17210593" author="zjffdu" created="Fri, 9 Oct 2020 03:59:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The workaround is to cancel the current running paragraph, and then the remaining paragraphs will be skipped.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17211856" author="olkkoti" created="Sun, 11 Oct 2020 09:02:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems that canceling the current paragraph is disabled on the frontend while whole note is running.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, runAllParagraph seems to block the websocket thread, which means that cancel requests are not handled while paragraphs are running. I have a pull request coming up, though I need to get &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3933&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3933&lt;/a&gt;&#160;merged first. &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Work in progress for this issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/olkkoti/zeppelin/commit/f234a954b791fa706c4e218e0d71035cfc543e2b&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/olkkoti/zeppelin/commit/f234a954b791fa706c4e218e0d71035cfc543e2b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
